4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were soiled:
1. Table holding grills (grease/food debris);
2. Sides of oven (grease);
3. Sides of fryers (grease);
4. Bottom inside silver freezer (food crumbs);
5. Large storage rack next to 2 part sink (general buildup/food debris);
6. Metal shelving across from 3 part sink (dust on lower shelves); 
7. Prep cooler - **crevice beneath compressor in the bottom (food debris/general buildup), **gaskets (crumbs); & **back edge of upper holding area (food debris); and 
8. Metal drawers across from fryers (general buildup).
Cleaning frequency was discussed. Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

4-602.13 General surfaces throughout the kitchen are in need of cleaning which include, but are not necessarily limited to, the following:
1. outside of rice storage bin (general buildup);
2. containers used for storage of spices and seasonings (food debris/general buildup);
3. handles of coolers (flour/general buildup);
4. bottom inside freezer by fryers (food debris)
5. around equipment on prep tables; and 
6. at the dish machine - the top of the machine, attached plumbing, and catch basin beneath plumbing (general buildup/food debris).
Clean the aforementioned items and all general surfaces as needed to eliminate buildup.
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.
